* TIMES.jl crafted case demo12_pfd (reference/crafted.toml, 13 Nov 2026): demo12_pfa (the
* REG1-REG2 power-flow grid with the allocation of generation and sectoral demand to grid
* nodes) plus a second grid node in REG1, so that powerflo.vda generates the demand allocation
* rows EQ_GR_DEMALL (L314-340; M1.3 change 27b-2), which no open model reaches:
* - TU_ELC_TRA1, a line with a reactance from ELC to the transport electricity TRAELC inside
*   REG1 (an intra-regional exchange), makes TRAELC a grid node beside ELC (L37-59);
* - sectoral demand fractions at both REG1 nodes become GR_DEMFR (L133-139), normalised over the
*   grid (L149-154); the node with the larger fraction is dropped from GR_DEMFR, and the other
*   gets GR_ADO and the EQ_GR_DEMALL rows (L155-162);
* - a generation fraction at TRAELC gives EQ_GR_GENALL rows at the second node too.
$ONEMPTY
$ONEPS
$ONWARNING
SET PRC
/
TU_ELC_TRA1
/

SET PRC_MAP
/
REG1.IRE.TU_ELC_TRA1
/

SET PRC_TSL
/
REG1.TU_ELC_TRA1.DAYNITE
/

SET PRC_ACTUNT
/
REG1.TU_ELC_TRA1.NRG.PJ
/

SET TOP_IRE
/
 REG1.ELC.REG1.TRAELC.TU_ELC_TRA1
/

SET PRC_DESC
/
 REG1.TU_ELC_TRA1 'Crafted: line from ELC to the transport electricity node (TIMES.jl demo12_pfd)'
/

PARAMETER PRC_REACT /
REG1.2005.TU_ELC_TRA1 0.1
/;

PARAMETER GR_ENDFR /
REG1.2005.TRAELC.RSDELC 0.4
REG1.2005.TRAELC.AGRELC 0.3
REG1.2020.TRAELC.AGRELC 0.5
/;

PARAMETER GR_GENFR /
REG1.2005.TRAELC.COA 0.5
REG1.2005.TRAELC.DIS 0.25
/;
